{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_versionpolicy", "label": "Version policy", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The honest assessment of what is stable, what is experimental and what to expect. Pre-1.0: the API is stable enough to build with, but expect breaking changes at minor bumps until 1.0."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_stabilitystatustable", "label": "Stability status overview", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## Status overview", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Core actor model, supervision, mailboxes/dispatchers, cluster membership, sharding, singleton, DistributedPubSub, DistributedData, PersistentActor, snapshot stores, migration adapters and broker actors are Stable; replicated event sourcing, worker mesh and Producer/ConsumerController are Experimental."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_semverpre10", "label": "Pre-1.0 versioning", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## Versioning until 1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Patch 0.x.Y is bug fixes only; minor 0.X.0 adds features and may include breaking changes; 1.0.0 is the API-stabilization commitment."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_semverpost10", "label": "Post-1.0 strict SemVer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## After 1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Patch for fixes, minor for backward-compatible additions, major for breaking changes with an explicit migration guide - a conservative cadence where major bumps are rare."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_stablemeaning", "label": "What 'stable' means here", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## What \"stable\" means here", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stable means the API is not expected to break, but pre-1.0 it may still gain optional parameters, new config sub-keys and additive return fields. Renaming or removing is not covered, and a break at a stable surface is flagged prominently in the CHANGELOG with a migration note."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_experimentalmeaning", "label": "What 'experimental' means", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## What \"experimental\" means", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Signatures may change, behavior may change in non-obvious ways, and performance is not yet optimized. Production use is fine - the maintainers use them - but expect to update code at minor bumps; a deeply experimental feature says so on its own page."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_deprecationpolicy", "label": "Deprecation policy: a hard cut pre-1.0", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## Deprecation policy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no guaranteed deprecation cycle: the old API can disappear in the same release that adds the new one. What you get instead is honesty - every breaking change carries a BREAKING marker and a one-line migration note in the CHANGELOG, and examples and docs are updated in the same change. Post-1.0 this tightens to a full major version of deprecation warning."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_securityfixesnobackport", "label": "Security fixes: no maintenance branches", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## Security fixes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Supported' means the latest published version and nothing else. A security fix lands on develop and ships in the next release; it is never backported to an earlier 0.x. SECURITY.md is also the scope boundary - the plaintext unauthenticated cluster-transport default is a documented default rather than a vulnerability, while a documented mitigation that fails to deliver is one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_pullrequestsnotaccepted", "label": "Pull requests are not accepted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## Reporting issues", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The issue tracker is the contribution channel - open a well-shaped issue and align on the approach there."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_roadmapitems", "label": "Specific roadmap items", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/version-policy.mdx", "source_location": "## Specific roadmap items", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OTel auto-instrumentation polish, more cluster transports (WebSocket, QUIC), sharding rebalance v2, more CRDT types - all additive."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_versionpolicy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_version_policy_stabilitystatustable", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_s